WebKit: the proxy of an ended web process is kept alive (and counted).

When the page of a process that ended (crashed, was terminated by the client, ran out of memory) is
loaded again in a new process, WebPageProxy::launchProcess releases the old WebProcessProxy. On this
port that destruction aborts the UI process: crashDueToCheckedPtrToDeadObject, from a CheckedPtr count of
the thread-safe kind (IPC::Connection::Client, which AuxiliaryProcessProxy implements) that is already
zero when a reference to it is released. Reproduced with LazyWeb+'s Stop or Reload on a page whose
process does not answer (issue #862): the UI process died right after launching the replacement process,
with the page's responsiveness calls of the embedder removed, with and without waiting for the socket to
close first. The cause is not found. Keeping the dead proxy (one reference leaked each time a process
ends) avoids it, and the embedder's `lzw_proxy_kept(pid, count)` says how many are kept.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebProcessProxy.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebProcessProxy.cpp
@@ -171,6 +171,9 @@
 
 #define WEBPROCESSPROXY_RELEASE_LOG_ERROR(channel, fmt, ...) RELEASE_LOG_ERROR(channel, "%p - [PID=%i] WebProcessProxy::" fmt, static_cast<const void*>(this), processID(), ##__VA_ARGS__)
 
+// The embedder's count of kept proxies (webkit/port/app/children.cpp); weak: other programs have none.
+extern "C" __attribute__((weak)) void lzw_proxy_kept(int pid, int kept);
+
 namespace WebKit {
 using namespace WebCore;
 
@@ -1462,6 +1465,21 @@
     // to be deleted before we can finish our work.
     Ref protectedThis { *this };
 
+    // LazyOS: the proxy of a process that ended is never destroyed. Destroying it (when the page is
+    // reloaded in a new process, which releases the old proxy) aborts the UI process in
+    // crashDueToCheckedPtrToDeadObject, a thread-safe CheckedPtr count that is already zero; seen on this
+    // port after WKPageTerminate and Reload (LazyWeb+, issue #862), with or without waiting for the
+    // socket to close first. The cause is not found; a dead proxy is a few kilobytes and a process ends
+    // only by a crash, a memory limit or the person's choice, so it is kept (a reference leaked once per
+    // ending) and counted: the embedder's hook says how many are kept.
+    ref();
+    {
+        static unsigned s_kept;
+        ++s_kept;
+        if (lzw_proxy_kept)
+            lzw_proxy_kept(static_cast<int>(processID()), static_cast<int>(s_kept));
+    }
+
     liveProcessesLRU().remove(*this);
 
     auto pages = mainPages();
